---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/ui/Icon.astro';
import Logo from '@/components/ui/Logo.astro';
import MondayContactForm from '@/components/forms/MondayContactForm.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Register Your Site - REDI Sites"
  description="Register your commercial property for a REDI readiness evaluation by the Site Selectors Guild."
  noindex
>
  <section class="bg-steel-100 pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div
        class="bg-steel-200/70 shadow-lifted relative mx-auto max-w-[580px] rounded-3xl px-6 py-8 sm:px-12 sm:py-10"
      >
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-ink-600 hover:text-ink-900 absolute top-6 right-6 transition-colors sm:top-8 sm:right-8"
          aria-label="Close and return home"
        >
          <Icon name="x" size={22} />
        </a>
        <Logo variant="nav" class="mx-auto" />

        <a
          href="/sign-in"
          class="font-heading text-ink-700 hover:text-ink-900 mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide uppercase transition-colors"
        >
          <Icon name="chevron-left" size={16} />
          Back
        </a>
        <h1 class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-[2.75rem]">Sign Up</h1>
        <p class="text-ink-600 mt-1 text-lg">Access REDI SITES tools &amp; value.</p>

        <div class="mt-6">
          <MondayContactForm formId="474841603e14828e7b565d097a98ad89" />
        </div>

        <!--
          TODO(auth): this form is a Monday.com lead-intake embed, not a
          real account-creation flow - there is still no self-serve account
          registration anywhere in this build. If/when that's built, this is
          where it goes. Nothing to reuse from SetPasswordForm.tsx besides
          the general form/validation pattern.
            1. Expected request:  POST /api/auth/register
               { email, password, name, company?, ...whatever fields the
               client wants collected - none are specified yet, this needs
               product input, not just engineering }.
            2. Role assignment: decide what WordPress user role a self-
               registered account gets by default (e.g. a restricted
               "member" role, not "subscriber"/"administrator") - must be
               enforced server-side; nothing here should let a client-
               supplied field set its own role.
            3. Expected response (success): 201 + either an auto-login
               session (see sign-in.astro TODO) or an "check your email to
               verify" flow - decide before building, this changes the UX
               significantly.
            4. Expected response (failure): 409 for "email already
               registered" (again, consider enumeration implications - see
               forgot-password.astro TODO), 422 for validation errors with
               field-level error detail.
            5. Add the same password-strength validation used in
               SetPasswordForm.tsx (`setPasswordSchema`, currently defined
               only in that file - consider extracting it to a shared
               `src/lib/validation/` module, which exists but is currently
               empty, once more than one form needs the same rules).
        -->
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
